From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henk Wiedig <henk@wiedig.de>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:54:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] drm/artosyn: dsi: timing from the mode
 (artosyn,timing-from-mode)

With artosyn,timing-from-mode the DSI line timing, lane rate and MIPI TX
PLL come from the mode, by the rule stock's dsi_set_timing applies to its
attrs: the line is the mode's htotal in lane byte clocks, rounded; the lane
rate makes that line exactly as long as the mode's; sync and back porch
scale with it; vertical in lines. For the LT9611EX's 1080p60 (2293x1125 at
154.7775 MHz) that is hsa 44, hbp 148, line 1720 at 928.8 Mbps, stock's
numbers; the same rule gives stock's nd043 panel numbers (32/32/1568 at
861.02 Mbps). The PLL word is Q8.24 of 4000 / Mbps (fits the captured
0x04a54972 and the recovered 891 Mbps word).

The D-PHY block per lane rate is stock's: dsi_set_timing() and
dphy_freq_conf_get2() of libmpp_service.so 2.1.4 run under qemu-aarch64
with the attrs of libpn_lt9611ex.so's modes (464, 478, 498, 928 and 972
Mbps: 1080p30, 720p60, 720p50, 1080p60, 1080p50). The same run with
libpn_nd043fhdm30p.so's attr reproduces the 861 Mbps block captured from
hardware word for word. CLKMGR_CFG goes with the rate.

The panel's other host settings stay (VID_MODE_CFG follows the DSI device's
mode flags, as for the panel). Without the property nothing changes.
